{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry things are running slowly today. I checked your desktop and it has plenty of free disk space, so that isn't the cause. To work out what's going on, could you tell me: 1) Is it only the shared drives that are slow, or are websites, Teams and email slow too? 2) Are coworkers near you seeing the same slowness? 3) Is it one particular shared drive or folder, or all of them? 4) Are you in the office on a wired connection, or working remotely on VPN or Wi-Fi? In the meantime, two things you can try: pause any big uploads or downloads (like OneDrive sync), and restart your desktop if it hasn't been restarted in a few days. If several people in your area are slow at the same time, let me know straight away and I'll send it to our network team.",
  "internal_note": "User 8, Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, CT hours 06:00-14:00. Device BL-DT-0108 (desktop): 78.1% disk free (400/512 GB), no warnings, so KB-017 is ruled out. The device shows OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-11T00:58Z. That could mean a connectivity problem on this machine or just that the agent check-in is stale. Worth a look if the slowness continues. Following KB-015, I asked: shares only or everything, whether others are affected, which share, and wired or VPN. Escalate if the whole office/site is slow, or if one share is slow for everyone (KB-015 escalation criteria). No actions queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-015",
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
